 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of triangles, as each triangle is processed once in a single draw call [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(W \times H \times D)$ for the voxel grid storage [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Voxelizing a whole scene at $512 \times 512 \times 512$ resolution took 11.70 ms on an NVIDIA GTX 770 without LOD or optimizations [S4, unofficial]. The $128^3$ grid is significantly faster [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Single-pass rendering (efficient), leverages highly optimized hardware rasterizer, simple implementation [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires conservative rasterization to avoid holes, fixed-resolution grid can be memory-intensive for high resolutions, order-independent writing requires careful handling of overwrites [S1, S4, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** Real-time global illumination, voxel cone tracing, volumetric effects where speed is prioritized over perfect geometric accuracy [S4, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of triangles, as each triangle is processed once in a single draw call [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(W \times H \times D)$ for the voxel grid storage [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Performance:** Voxelizing a whole scene at $512 \times 512 \times 512$ resolution took 11.70 ms on an NVIDIA GTX 770 without LOD or optimizations [S5, unofficial]. The $128^3$ grid is significantly faster [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** Single-pass rendering (efficient), leverages highly optimized hardware rasterizer, simple implementation [S5, unofficial].
